  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated food security project in Kassala, Sudan (IFSP-Kassala)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Considering the challenging food-gap and the nutritional status of the targeted population the projects overall goal (or Ultimate Outcome) has been defined as: &quot;Improved food and nutrition security of the targeted population in Kassala, especially for women and youth.&quot; In order to contribute to the achievement of this goal three interlinked components have been identified, namely:  Component 1: &quot;Agricultural Production &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; Productivity&quot;  Component 2: &quot;Employment and Livelihood Opportunities&quot;  Component 3: &quot;Community Participation &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; Empowerment&quot;  While component 1 and 2 are linked together and complement each other within the context of a value-chain perspective, component 3 provides the entry point whilst at the same time ensures sustainability.</narrative>
  </description>
